  "id": "Compound::DB08899 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Enzalutamide is classified as an androgen receptor antagonist, and its relationship with Cyp2c19 is mediated through its inclusion in a broader class of androgen receptor antagonists. This class includes Bicalutamide, Nilutamide, and Flutamide, all of which are known to bind to Cyp2c19. The evidence suggests that Enzalutamide, through its inclusion in this class, may exert a modulatory effect on Cyp2c19 activity. The lowest common ancestors of Enzalutamide and its class members, such as (Trifluoromethyl)Benzenes, indicate a shared structural feature that could influence enzyme binding or metabolic activity. The varying scores across the paths reflect the strength of the evidence, with Enzalutamide showing the highest confidence in its relationship with Cyp2c19. The mechanism appears to involve the interaction of these compounds with Cyp2c19, potentially through shared binding sites or structural similarities, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
